Feature: DeleteTopics validates names UUIDs duplicates and authorized identity collisions
  Scenario Outline: Invalid identity rows are excluded once each while authorized aliases remain private
    Given DeleteTopics uses <format> rows <request> and denies names <denied>
    When deletion resolves topic identities and rejects names also supplied by authorized UUID
    Then the ordered deletable topic identities are <topics>
    And the ordered invalid deletion rows are <invalid>
    Examples:
      | case                                         | format | request                                                                                 | denied | topics                            | invalid                                                                                      |
      | a name row and an id row                     | UUID   | orders/zero;null/other                                                                  | none   | orders/name/zero;null/id/other    | none                                                                                         |
      | neither name nor id                          | UUID   | null/zero                                                                               | none   | none                              | null/zero/no-name-or-id                                                                      |
      | both name and id                             | UUID   | orders/orders                                                                           | none   | none                              | orders/orders/name-and-id                                                                    |
      | an empty name with an id                     | UUID   | empty/orders                                                                            | none   | none                              | empty/orders/name-and-id                                                                     |
      | an empty name without an id                  | UUID   | empty/zero                                                                              | none   | empty/name/zero                   | none                                                                                         |
      | a name three times                           | UUID   | orders/zero;orders/zero;orders/zero                                                     | none   | none                              | orders/zero/duplicate-name                                                                   |
      | a legacy name twice                          | legacy | orders,other,orders                                                                     | none   | other/name/zero                   | orders/zero/duplicate-name                                                                   |
      | interleaved duplicates                       | UUID   | b/zero;null/other;a/zero;null/orders;b/zero;null/other;a/zero;c/zero;null/orders;b/zero | none   | c/name/zero                       | b/zero/duplicate-name;a/zero/duplicate-name;null/other/duplicate-id;null/orders/duplicate-id |
      | an id twice                                  | UUID   | null/orders;null/orders                                                                 | none   | none                              | null/orders/duplicate-id                                                                     |
      | a name an authorized id also names           | UUID   | null/orders;orders/zero                                                                 | none   | none                              | orders/orders/name-of-id                                                                     |
      | a duplicate id and the name of that id       | UUID   | null/orders;orders/zero;null/orders                                                     | none   | none                              | null/orders/duplicate-id;orders/orders/name-of-id                                            |
      | a collision with a denied name stays private | UUID   | null/orders;orders/zero                                                                 | orders | orders/id/orders;orders/name/zero | none                                                                                         |
